    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0178" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.001 Roosevelt, F. D./9453½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President, the Secretary of
                        State, and the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d127-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-14T17:00:00+02:00">November 14, 1943—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1869. Most secret for the President, the Secretary and the Under Secretary.</p>
                <p>In expressing his keen pleasure with President Roosevelt’s letter of October 26
                    to President Inönü,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d127-f2"/> the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs<anchor n="3" xml:id="d127-f3"/> remarked to me last night that Inönü
                    would be delighted to meet our President and that if President Roosevelt could
                    not be persuaded to visit Turkey, he would be more than pleased to go to meet
                    him should he visit any other part of the Near East.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d127-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d127-f1-content">
                <p>On November 17, 1943, the White House Map Room telegraphed a paraphrase of this
                    message to Greer, “to be held for delivery to the President upon arrival at
                    Oran.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d127-f2" n="2" xml:id="d127-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg43">p. 43</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d127-f3" n="3" xml:id="d127-f3-content">
                <p>Numan Menemencioğlu.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
